# Push and deploy (NVCCZ VPS)

When the user says **"push and deploy the changes"** (or similar), follow this sequence end-to-end.

## 1. Git (local)

1. Commit any uncommitted work if the user expects it included.
2. `git push origin master` (or current branch they specify).

## 2. VPS deploy

Credentials and host: read `.cursor/deploy-vps.credentials.local` (gitignored).

| Setting | Value |
|---------|--------|
| SSH | `root@31.220.82.129` |
| Projects root | `/var/www/projects` |

Run on the VPS (single SSH session or chained remote commands):

```bash
cd /var/www/projects/nts
git pull
npm i
npm run build

cd /var/www/projects/client1
git pull
npm i
npm run build

pm2 restart all
```

**Order matters:** `nts` (dev) first, then `client1` (prod), then `pm2 restart all`.

## 3. Verify

- Confirm each `git pull` and `npm run build` succeeded (exit code 0).
- Confirm `pm2 restart all` completed.
- Optionally curl dev API health if user cares (`https://dev-api.arcus.co.zw/health`).

## Notes

- Do **not** commit `.cursor/deploy-vps.credentials.local`.
- On Windows, use `ssh` with password via `sshpass` if available, or `plink`/interactive SSH; prefer one remote heredoc/script to avoid multiple password prompts.
- Helper script (optional): `bash scripts/deploy-vps-remote.sh` documents the remote commands.
